---
import BaseLayout from "~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About the platform-agnostic email spec"
  description="Learn how The Email Specification turns scattered RFCs, accessibility guidance, and provider requirements into one testable, open checklist."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>One map of the email stack</h1><p class="lede">
        Email is a chain of formats, DNS records, relays, filters, clients, and human
        expectations. This project turns that chain into an auditable contract.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <article class="narrow section prose">
    <h2>What this is</h2><p>
      A provider-agnostic specification of observable outcomes. Each page states what the
      requirement is, why it matters, how to implement it, common mistakes, and how to
      verify the delivered result.
    </p>
    <h2>What this is not</h2><p>
      It is not an ESP comparison, a template framework, legal advice, or a guarantee of
      inbox placement. Standards define the floor; mailbox providers and recipients still
      make their own decisions.
    </p>
    <h2>Open by design</h2><p>
      Code is MIT licensed. Specification content is CC BY 4.0. Every topic cites its
      sources and the repository accepts corrections.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
